Chapter: BvtLoanRetire
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter EconomyCurrencyValid
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtSealLoans
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-246: each day an empty shop borrows a gold from the king, a customer pays it one, it repays in full and spends
 its till back to the customer, and a seal closes the day. 300 days lend 300 loans, more than the 128 a loan block
 holds: each seal retires the repaid loan, so the only live loan is the customer's float, the tables never grow, ids
 keep counting, and twenty days retain no heap early or late (a loan table growth, the control, retains some).
  blr-day : EuCurrency, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  blr-day (x) (shop) (payer) = let purse = (ep-actor x.world shop).purse
    in let lent = bb-borrow-one x shop
    in let paid = eu-pay x True payer purse 0 0 1
    in let repaid = bb-repay x shop
    in let spent = eu-pay x True purse payer (em-purse x.copper purse).coin (em-purse x.silver purse).coin (em-purse x.world.money purse).coin
    in let sealed = eu-seal x
    in if lent == 1 & paid == 0 & spent == 0 & bb-debt x.world.money purse 0 == 0 & sealed == 0 & x.world.money.loan-count == 1 then 1 else 0
  blr-days : EuCurrency, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  blr-days (x) (shop) (payer) (left) (done) = if left == 0 then done else blr-days x shop payer (left - 1) (done + blr-day x shop payer)
 The shop and the customer's purse, after the customer is staked a 2-gold float and the shop is emptied; empty when
 the fixture fails.
  blr-setup : EuCurrency -> List Integer
  blr-setup (x) = let opened = bsl-open x
    in let shop = cg-label-actor x 1001
    in let customer = cg-label-actor x 1002
    in if shop < 1 | customer < 1 then []
    else let purse = (ep-actor x.world shop).purse
    in let payer = (ep-actor x.world customer).purse
    in let drained = eu-pay x True purse 1 (em-purse x.copper purse).coin (em-purse x.silver purse).coin (em-purse x.world.money purse).coin
    in let staked = eu-lend x True 1 payer 3 2 0 em-limit
    in if staked < 1 | cgf-value x purse /= 0 then [] else [shop, payer]
  bvt-loan-retire : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-loan-retire (unused) = when bb-economy 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("loan retirement fixture economy: " & e) False
    is Ok (x) -> act
      setup <- blr-setup x
      ok <- list-length setup == 2
      shop <- if ok then list-at setup 0 else 0
      payer <- if ok then list-at setup 1 else 0
      length <- list-length x.world.money.loans
      warm <- if ok then blr-days x shop payer 20 0 else 0
      h0 <- __heap-save
      early <- if ok then blr-days x shop payer 20 0 else 0
      h1 <- __heap-save
      middle <- if ok then blr-days x shop payer 240 0 else 0
      h2 <- __heap-save
      late <- if ok then blr-days x shop payer 20 0 else 0
      h3 <- __heap-save
      days <- warm + early + middle + late
      a <- bvt-check ("UOAIX-246 retirement: days " & show days & ", live " & show x.world.money.loan-count & ", grown " & show (list-length x.world.money.loans - length) & ", next " & show x.world.money.loan-next & ", heap days 21-40 " & show (h1 - h0) & " days 281-300 " & show (h3 - h2) & ", opening extra " & show (em-open-held x.world.money)) ok
      b <- bvt-check "UOAIX-246: 300 days of borrow, full repayment and a seal each lend 300 loans past the 128 a block holds, and each seal retires the repaid one: one live loan, no table growth, no extra opening cells" (ok & days == 300 & x.world.money.loan-count == 1 & list-length x.world.money.loans == length & em-open-held x.world.money == 0)
      c <- bvt-check "UOAIX-246: loan ids keep counting across the retirements (the float is 1, the shop's 300 loans 2 to 301)" (ok & x.world.money.loan-next == 301)
      h4 <- __heap-save
      grown <- eu-grow-loans x
      h5 <- __heap-save
      d <- bvt-check ("UOAIX-246: twenty days early and late retain no heap, where one loan table growth retains " & show (h5 - h4) & " bytes") (ok & h1 - h0 == 0 & h3 - h2 == 0 & h5 - h4 > 0)
      e <- bvt-check "UOAIX-246: the economy validates after 300 seals" (ok & euv-valid x)
      a + b + c + d + e
    end